.TH elfshaker-gc 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-gc \- Delete redundant loose snapshots and unreferenced loose objects.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker gc\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-loose\-snapshots\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-loose\-objects\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reclaims data\-directory space after snapshots have been packed. At least one of \-\-loose\-snapshots or \-\-loose\-objects is required. When both are selected, redundant loose snapshot indexes are removed before object reachability is calculated.
.PP
Packed data is not deleted. Use \-\-dry\-run to inspect the deletion set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would be deleted without changing the data directory.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-snapshots\fR
Delete loose snapshot indexes whose snapshots also exist in a pack.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-objects\fR
Delete loose objects not referenced by a remaining loose snapshot.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
